<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n92343" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥῆξις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>, ἡ, 
			Aeol.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ϝρῆξις</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Alc.
			149
		</span></i>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>breaking,
				bursting</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φλεβίου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Aph.</u>
					4.78
				</span></i>
			; sc. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀστέου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>VC</u>
					12
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλευμόνων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Ir.</u>
					p.28
				</span></i>
			 W. (pl.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμπύρους τ᾽ ἀκμὰς
				ῥήξεις τε</span>, i.e. both the pointed flames and the
				<i>broken</i> (the former a good omen, the latter bad), <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1256
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ ῥῆξιν νέφους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Mu.</u>
					394b17
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Stoic.</u>
				1.34
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀέρος ῥ</span>., as the effect
			of a mighty shout, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Flam.</u>
				10
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>breaking forth</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν καταμηνίων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Aph.</u>
					3.28
				</span></i>
			 (pl.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἵματος ῥ. διὰ ῥινῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Prog.</u>
					7
				</span></i>
			; <i>discharge</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Aph.</u>
				5.15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Epid.</u>
				6.6.12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>rent, cleft</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.935c
			</span></i> (pl.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥήξεις ἐν τοῖς τείχεσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					<u>Bel.</u>
					84.22
				</span></i>
			.</div>
